  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_016, multimodal/singleprofile/pca/resnet50/concat, acc 0.527) shows that RNA is the dominant signal and adding ResNet50 image features gives a modest ~4% boost over RNA-only. However, the profile axis (single vs. multi) is completely unexplored across all four experiments, representing the largest remaining uncertainty in the design space. Question: config_018 extends config_016 by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) constant. Because aggregation is a necessary consequence of multiprofile, this isolates a single design decision—whether multiple profiles improve the representation. Why best next experiment: If multiprofile helps, it opens the aggregation axis (avgpool vs. transformer) and confirms a promising direction for further exploitation. If it does not, we can eliminate ~30 multiprofile configurations and refocus on RNA encoder (scvi, scgpt) or image encoder (ViT-L) variations. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental axis is more informative than testing a secondary encoder swap that might be confounded by an unexplored profile/aggregation interaction."
}

